From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:25:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 66/99] v8: e2k: baseline code counts the interrupt budget in
 64 bits

The budget was loaded, added to and tested as a 32-bit value: load and
sign extension, 32-bit sum and sign extension, compare. The result of a
32-bit operation reaches a 64-bit one four cycles later than that of a
64-bit one, and this runs on every back edge and every return of baseline
code. The budget and the weights are far from the ends of int32: the sum
is made in 64 bits, its low half is stored as before.
---
 chromium/v8/src/baseline/e2k/baseline-assembler-e2k-inl.h | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chromium/v8/src/baseline/e2k/baseline-assembler-e2k-inl.h b/chromium/v8/src/baseline/e2k/baseline-assembler-e2k-inl.h
index 81a0cc8e5d..1bb7dbdce9 100644
--- a/chromium/v8/src/baseline/e2k/baseline-assembler-e2k-inl.h
+++ b/chromium/v8/src/baseline/e2k/baseline-assembler-e2k-inl.h
@@ -755,7 +755,9 @@ void BaselineAssembler::AddToInterruptBudgetAndJumpIfNotExceeded(
   __ Ld_w(interrupt_budget,
           FieldMemOperand(feedback_cell,
                           offsetof(FeedbackCell, interrupt_budget_)));
-  __ Add_w(interrupt_budget, interrupt_budget, weight);
+  // In 64 bits: the budget and the weights are far from the ends of int32,
+  // and a 32-bit sum waits four cycles for its sign extension.
+  __ Add_d(interrupt_budget, interrupt_budget, Operand(weight));
   __ St_w(interrupt_budget,
           FieldMemOperand(feedback_cell,
                           offsetof(FeedbackCell, interrupt_budget_)));
@@ -775,7 +777,7 @@ void BaselineAssembler::AddToInterruptBudgetAndJumpIfNotExceeded(
   __ Ld_w(interrupt_budget,
           FieldMemOperand(feedback_cell,
                           offsetof(FeedbackCell, interrupt_budget_)));
-  __ Add_w(interrupt_budget, interrupt_budget, weight);
+  __ add_d(interrupt_budget, interrupt_budget, weight);
   __ St_w(interrupt_budget,
           FieldMemOperand(feedback_cell,
                           offsetof(FeedbackCell, interrupt_budget_)));
